+**There is a third chain, and it disagrees.** `lib/unplacehold.js` — which
+serves only the legacy plaintext-auth `POST /unplacehold` route — carries its
+own private copy of every formatter: `phone`, `email_mask`, `upper`, and since
+2026-09-24 `ssn_mask` / `ssn_last4`. **Add a modifier to one chain and the
+other does not get it.** The two also disagree on an **empty source value**:
+`resolverService` treats empty as UNRESOLVED and leaves the raw
+`{{table.column}}` standing, while `unplacehold` resolves it to `''`. That
+divergence is generic, not SSN-specific, and long pre-dates the SSN work;
+`tests/ssnModifiers.test.js` pins it rather than fixing it. A THIRD copy of
+the SSN masking lives in `services/esignPrefillService.js` (`ssnMasked`), for
+e-sign prefill. Unifying the three is filed in `ref/plans.md`.
+
 The distinction is not cosmetic: the two resolvers were built for different jobs. The universal resolver fetches live DB rows and is deliberately soft-fail and visible, because it renders text a human will read and a broken token should be obvious. The workflow resolver walks an in-memory variable store, is used on machine config (URLs, ids, JSON bodies) as well as prose, and blanks unknowns so a half-resolved URL doesn't get called.
 
